  "heights": {
    "description": "A grid is only laid out where every card fits its cell: its lowest row must be at least rowHeightPx high, so the viewport must be at least chromeHeightPx (the navigation bar above the overview) + rowHeightPx × (sum of the row weights ÷ the smallest row weight) high, rounded up — else the learner swipes through that grid one page at a time, as on a phone (mode swipe). Widths and heights are measured in the learner's text size: at a text scale s every threshold is s times as large (a breakpoint b becomes floor(b × s), a least height h becomes floor(h × s)). Each vector is a viewport in px, a text scale, and the grid and mode it gets with the nine pages of four quizzes.",
    "rowHeightPx": 160,
    "chromeHeightPx": 56,
    "minimum": { "desktop": 600, "tablet": 856 },
